An index (`guidance.always-on-is-an-index`): one line per item; the detail is in
the named skill, rule (`aval rule <id>`), amont-agent rule, or memory file.

## Git stash policy (worktrees)

- `refs/stash` is shared by every worktree: run `git stash list` and pick your
  entry by its message before any stash operation (amont-agent `bare-stash-pop`).
- To set work aside, prefer a WIP commit; else `git stash push -u -m <tag>`, then
  `git stash apply <sha>` of that entry, then drop it.

## Git worktree isolation for agent work

- Do edit and commit work in a per-task worktree from `origin/main` — the
  `worktree-task` skill (start, plan commit, verification, finish, teardown).

## Git hygiene

- Name the repository in each mutating git command (`git -C <repo>` or a subshell
  `(cd <repo> && …)`): a bare `cd` carries into the next call, batched siblings included.
- Run `git status` before every commit and stage explicit paths (amont-agent `git-add-broad`).
- Release: commit, check HEAD advanced, then tag, then push the tag — the
  `tag-release` skill. A tag is never force-pushed; a fix gets the next version.
- Commit subjects: ≤ 50 characters, conventional prefix, no emoji (a hook adds it).
- AGENTS.md generated block (`guidance.generated-block-rides-the-change`): `amont.fix`
  is unset here, so run `amont agents-md` in the task worktree and stage it.
  Never run `amont-fleet fix --apply --agents-md` on the live checkouts.
- Add the `Co-Authored-By: Claude` trailer only on the user's own repos; for
  upstream or third-party repos, leave it out (ask when unsure).

## Before pushing / declaring CI green

- Run the project's checks locally first (`work.verification-loop-before-push`).
- Read a run's `conclusion` explicitly; `gh run watch --exit-status` can exit 0 on
  a failure — the `merge-when-green` skill.
- Assert that each scripted bulk-edit replacement landed: a non-matching replace
  exits 0.
- Run a mutating command bare and check its effect, never through `tail`/`head`
  (amont-agent `pipe-to-tail`; `relais-verified-push` for pushes).
- Web/UI work is done when the rendered result is checked in a real browser (Chrome
  MCP or Playwright), not on CI green or a bundle grep.
- A page for the person to look at opens in their default browser (`open '<url>'`),
  never in chrome-devtools MCP / Playwright / headless Chrome — those are the agent's.
- For a reported visual bug, reproduce the user's exact view (route, mode, zoom,
  state) before the fix and again after the deploy.

## Repo ownership / PR workflow

- Land work through a pull request; a hook refuses pushes to `main` and
  `--no-verify` is refused (`general.no-disabled-safety`).
- An approved plan is carried to production without asking — merge, release,
  deploy, observe (`work.agent-lands-the-plan`, ADR-0029); ask only what it left open.
- Merge your own PRs on green CI and an approved review — the `merge-when-green`
  skill (`work.merge-on-green`); `gh pr merge --auto` is refused (amont-agent).
- Confirm destructive steps the plan does not name (`work.ask-only-what-the-plan-left-open`).

## Forgejo API ({{ .forge.host }})

- Both credentials are required: the mTLS cert `~/.config/mtls/{{ .forge.slug }}-client.{crt,key}`
  (missing → curl HTTP 000) and the token in `~/.netrc` — the curl recipe is in `forgejo-recipes`.
- Probe `/repos/{owner}/{repo}` to test access; `/api/v1/user` 403s on this token's
  scope. Never echo the token into output, a commit or a PR body; pass it in `$TOK`.
  More: the `reference_forgejo_*` memories.

## Shell environment

- The Bash tool runs zsh 5.9: write bash-compatible syntax, never fish
  (`claude_code_bash_tool_runs_zsh_not_fish.md`).
- zsh traps are guarded by amont-agent (`equals-separator`, `glob-in-flag-value`,
  `glob-no-match`); `status` is read-only — name the variable `rc`.
- `grep` is ugrep with `--ignore-files`: a recursive grep skips gitignored paths;
  name the directory or pass `--no-ignore-files`. `find` is bfs; sed and coreutils
  are GNU; awk, xargs, tar and diff are BSD; `stat -f '%…'` succeeds with a wrong answer.

## Reading files (overrides the bypass-mode default)

- Read files with the Read tool, windowed on large ones; search with Grep/Glob;
  trust Edit/Write results (amont-agent `whole-file-dump`, `read-unbounded-large`,
  `file-reread`, `persisted-output-dump`).

## Working method

- Plans, review panel, implementation review, verification and previews:
  `work.*` rules (ADR-0022/0023/0028) — run `/plan-review` before ExitPlanMode.
- When a decision is the person's, offer 2–4 options, recommendation first
  (`work.human-decisions-offer-options`).
- Triage: one sentence → code; one session with every decision statable →
  plan mode + panel; more sessions or unstatable decisions → a programme map
  (`programme` skill, `work.programme-map`).
- Before a worktree, a diagnosis or a release, check who works there:
  `amont-agent board --repo <r>` (`work.board-before-starting`).

## Relais routing

- Route bounded implementation or inspection tasks through relais — the
  `relais:relais` skill; say in one line which path each task took.

## Security

- When a secret rides in a URL, also clamp the HTTP client's own loggers
  (`httpx`, `urllib3`, `botocore`) to WARNING; check reprs, tracebacks and spans too.

## Communication style

- Mention an open action item once, and again only when its context changes.
